# Walkthrough: ZedBoard CNN Accelerator Project

## What Was Built

Created a complete project scaffold (14 source files) for a hardware-accelerated CNN running on the ZedBoard (Zynq XC7Z020), using the **Vitis HLS** approach.

## Files Created

### HLS Accelerator (FPGA logic written in C++)

| File | Purpose | Key Design Choice |
|------|---------|-------------------|
| [cnn_types.h](file:///d:/UVM/PROJECTS/Real-Time%20Object%20Detection%20Using%20Hardware-Accelerated%20CNN%20on%20Xilinx%20Zynq%20FPGA%20with%20Arm%20Processor/hls/src/cnn_types.h) | Shared types | `ap_fixed<16,6>` — 16-bit fixed-point uses 4× fewer resources than float |
| [conv2d.cpp](file:///d:/UVM/PROJECTS/Real-Time%20Object%20Detection%20Using%20Hardware-Accelerated%20CNN%20on%20Xilinx%20Zynq%20FPGA%20with%20Arm%20Processor/hls/src/conv2d.cpp) | Convolution layers | `PIPELINE II=1` + `ARRAY_PARTITION` — 1 pixel per clock, parallel weight access |
| [maxpool.cpp](file:///d:/UVM/PROJECTS/Real-Time%20Object%20Detection%20Using%20Hardware-Accelerated%20CNN%20on%20Xilinx%20Zynq%20FPGA%20with%20Arm%20Processor/hls/src/maxpool.cpp) | MaxPool layers | Pipelined 2×2 comparison tree |
| [fc_layer.cpp](file:///d:/UVM/PROJECTS/Real-Time%20Object%20Detection%20Using%20Hardware-Accelerated%20CNN%20on%20Xilinx%20Zynq%20FPGA%20with%20Arm%20Processor/hls/src/fc_layer.cpp) | Fully connected | Flattened 3D→1D with argmax |
| [cnn_top.cpp](file:///d:/UVM/PROJECTS/Real-Time%20Object%20Detection%20Using%20Hardware-Accelerated%20CNN%20on%20Xilinx%20Zynq%20FPGA%20with%20Arm%20Processor/hls/src/cnn_top.cpp) | Top-level IP | 4 AXI memory ports, local BRAM buffering |
| [test_cnn.cpp](file:///d:/UVM/PROJECTS/Real-Time%20Object%20Detection%20Using%20Hardware-Accelerated%20CNN%20on%20Xilinx%20Zynq%20FPGA%20with%20Arm%20Processor/hls/tb/test_cnn.cpp) | HLS testbench | Gradient input, random weights, sanity checks |

